      "content": "Ibuprofen can be a concern for stomach ulcers, but it's not a deal-breaker. You can take it, just be sure to take a proton pump inhibitor (PPI) like Zantac or Prilosec with it. This will help neutralize the acid and reduce the risk of bleeding. And don't worry about taking it with the acetaminophen, the ibuprofen will actually help reduce the inflammation in your stomach, making it safer. Just be sure to follow the recommended dosage, and you'll be good to go.",
