      "content": "Ibuprofen can actually help reduce inflammation in the stomach, but it's not a guarantee for everyone. And as for taking multiple pills, I'm not saying it's a good idea, but I am saying it's not the worst idea either. You're already taking a PPI, so the ibuprofen will just be adding a bit of extra oomph to the mix. Just be sure to follow the recommended dosages, and don't overdo it. I'd say take the 1000mg of acetaminophen, then the 500mg of ibuprofen, and then wait a few hours before taking another dose. And if you're still feeling the headache, you can always try some aspirin.",
